## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond the one, or a byte of `DEPLOY.md`, `support.ts`, a product/config/package/lock file = **Blocker**; a second commit = moved head (STOP); a person's name, real customer name or secret in an added line or message = **Blocker**; a decision-card slug = **Blocker**; an assertion removed or loosened = **Major**; a work number or shape id in an added title or comment, or a ticket key in the PR title = **Minor**.
- **G-2 kill-lost (C2).** Old flags + pty fails + new does not = **Major, class** (`NO GO round 1 of 2`); the new scanner reds the real `DEPLOY.md` (list not empty) = **Major, class**; a shape neither flags that a pty fails = **Note** (fact quoted; the builder's Deferred E11 and X19 are expected Notes); old flags, new does not, no pty failure = **Note** (listed); new flags, no bash failure = **Note**.
- **G-3 closure (C3).** A named row (the 12) red under no revert or swap = **Major, class**; a revert that turns more or fewer rows red than the builder claimed = **Minor** (name them) unless a named row is lost, then Major; the 16 original rows red under a swap = a finding at the severity of its cause; a guard row red under none = **Minor**; the new plant not failing in bash 5.2 = **Major** (the comment claims more than a shell does, the very item 5); a builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 stability and names (C4).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; file other than 31 of 31 or group other than 490 without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 15 = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major**.
- **G-5 CI, CodeQL, claims (C5, C6).** A failing check-run on the head or merge result = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS; an analysis of the head missing = NOT scanned; an open alert on the head or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with #93, #92, #91, #86, #85 or another live lane = **Major**; a merge ref still on other parents after 10 minutes of polling = a Note (recompute in your clone) and `CI pending: merge ref`; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact.
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table.** Any Major or Blocker of the class (G-2, G-3) = `NO GO round 1 of 2` (a builder fix and one more gate remain). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows and any Minor). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read 11-12 at the draft: expect to wait). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, any vitest over more than one file, the group run, the pty containers in a batch. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the C2 harness, the clone, C5 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b699/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b699/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate (G129 runs containers on the same daemon: wait for it, do not race it). A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b699/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b699-node:head` once: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b699-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`); record node, npm, vitest versions (RELAYED: v22.23.2, 10.9.8, 5.0.0). One image serves main and head (the trees differ in one test file). The mutant sweeps and the corpus may run db-free in the image (same vitest args, no postgres) once you have shown the db-free per-row results of the head file equal its `dbone.sh` results; the 3x file runs and the group run go through `dbone.sh`. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b699-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name. Budget: about 14 container starts (baseline file, baseline group, head file 3x, group, db-free sweep batches, pty batches).

